# Format And Clippy Before Commit

Before creating any git commit that includes Rust sources (`.rs` files), verify
workspace formatting and Clippy so CI does not fail:

```sh
cargo fmt --all -- --check
cargo clippy --workspace -- -D warnings
```

If `cargo fmt` reports diffs:

1. Run `cargo fmt --all`
2. Stage the reformatted files with the commit
3. Re-run both checks and confirm they pass

Do this **before** `git commit`, as part of the commit prep (alongside status/diff/log),
not as a follow-up CI fix commit when it could have been caught locally.

The repo also ships `.githooks/pre-commit` (enable with
`git config core.hooksPath .githooks`) which runs the same checks when `.rs`
files are staged. Still run the checks yourself when preparing a commit; do not
rely only on the hook (for example when using environments that skip hooks).

Skip only when the commit contains no `.rs` files (for example docs-only or
`.cursor/rules` changes).
